 "known_issues": [
  "Synthetic: generated by CAMBER's own model of a VAV system, not measured. It shows what the rules see, not how a real system behaves; never cite it as evidence about real buildings.",
  "The resets take one trim-and-respond cycle per trended hour, so reset_effectiveness reconstructs them exactly. A real controller cycles every few minutes; on an hourly trend of one, the rule's reconstruction is coarse.",
  "The fleet rules (the rogue-zone and cohort-starvation censuses, cohort_airflow, cohort_space_temp, zones_heat_cool_census) report one finding for the whole facility, on <fleet>: camber datasets score cannot score them, and the census rules group the boxes under their air handler only through a served-by topology (the run template declares one).",
  "ZN{n}_FLOW_MIN, the box's minimum airflow setpoint, is mapped to airflow_sp, the role of the box's active airflow setpoint: the data has no active setpoint. reheat_minimization_g36 and zones_heat_cool_census read airflow_sp as the minimum when no airflow_min_sp is mapped, as here. The static-pressure census compares airflow with it too, where G36 compares it with the box's active airflow setpoint, so it counts fewer 2- and 3-request cycles than the air handler's own DSP_REQ.",
  "The SAT rogue-zone census counts only a box's 2- and 3-request cycles (the zone 3 and 5 F over its cooling setpoint); the air handler's SAT_REQ also counts a box's cooling loop over 95 %, which the box does not trend (the census counts it from zone_cool_loop where one is mapped)."
